t;Adjudicator&quot; that is not in bold, like the other one (the third one)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1841-nflagey","name":"nflagey","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-29T20:25:52-08:00","id":39074,"title":"","content":"Just flipping through:<br /> PDF page 358, 360, 362, 364, 366, 370, 378, 384, 386, 388: the headers for each page of the adventure say &quot;How And Angel Dies&quot; instead of &quot;How An Angel Dies.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-29T20:29:28-08:00","id":39076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/38920-demon-errata?p=39030#post39030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>p. 16:</b> Mr. Gone's name is spelt &quot;<b>Chrs</b>&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, the &quot;Character Sheet Design&quot; part isn't bolded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-29T21:10:27-08:00","id":39100,"title":"","content":"There's no character sheet. It's listed in the index as being on pages 394-395, but that's still the index. After that, it's the back cover.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-29T21:56:42-08:00","id":39131,"title":"","content":"Page 109 mentions that Aether can enhance physical characteristics, but I haven't been able to find any table or indication for this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/89-quatren","name":"Quatren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-29T23:16:37-08:00","id":39185,"title":"","content":"The cost to raise Primum at character creation differs between page 87 (5 merit dots = 1 dot of Primum) and pages 80, 81, 88 (3 merit dots = 1 dot of Primum).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1231-gapb","name":"gapb","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-30T01:21:35-08:00","id":39239,"title":"","content":"Very nice book btw!<br /> <br /> I found a few layout things with on the mend embed:<br /> &quot;success&quot; and &quot;exceptional success&quot; are not bolded. And after exceptional success (text) there is no . at the end of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-30T11:26:29-08:00","id":39495,"title":"","content":"Page 26: &quot;The Matrix and its sequels The Matrix Reloaded and The Matrix Revolutions are as subtle as a brick in the face, but showcase <b>both </b>the paranoia of resistance fighters in a world completely controlled by their enemy.&quot;<br /> <br /> Silly <i>Demon!</i> You can't have a &quot;both&quot; without an &quot;and&quot;!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/134196/Chuubos-Marvelous-WishGranting-Engine\" target=\"_blank\">Chuubo's Marvelous Wish-Granting Engine RPG</a> \u2014 <a href=\"http://www.patreon.com/JennaMoran\" target=\"_blank\">Jenna Moran's Patreon</a> \u2014 <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/215-rand-brittain","name":"Rand Brittain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-30T15:06:09-08:00","id":39620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rand Brittain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/38920-demon-errata?p=39495#post39495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Page 26: &quot;The Matrix and its sequels The Matrix Reloaded and The Matrix Revolutions are as subtle as a brick in the face, but showcase <b>both </b>the paranoia of resistance fighters in a world completely controlled by their enemy.&quot;<br /> <br /> Silly <i>Demon!</i> You can't have a &quot;both&quot; without an &quot;and&quot;!</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps the sentence was supposed to be &quot;but both showcase\u2026&quot; rather than &quot;but showcase both\u2026&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1231,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1231-gapb","user":"gapb","date":".  clarification 12-30-2013, 06:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1231-gapb","name":"gapb","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-30T15:49:33-08:00","id":39651,"title":"","content":"p.193 Duration for pacts:<br /> The whole first paragraph is bold (not sure if intended).<br /> &quot;bydestroying&quot; has no space in between....beginning of the 3rd line","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-30T19:20:22-08:00","id":39737,"title":"","content":"Consider moving the &quot;Incarnations&quot; and &quot;Agendas&quot; pages (currently 34 and 35) to Chapter Two, or at least somewhere where they won't interrupt the flow of the text quite so jarringly.<br /> <br /> p. 39: &quot;...whatever it takes together impressionable humans...&quot; I'm pretty sure that should be &quot;...whatever it takes <b>to gather</b> impressionable humans...&quot;<br /> p. 40: &quot;Many demons look at shoring up <b>with</b> [should be &quot;a&quot;] Cover in the same way that humans view saving <b>moneyor</b> [missing space] undertaking home repairs: as insurance against potential misfortune&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1856,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1856-hakkonen","user":"Hakkonen","date":". 12-30-2013, 11:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1856-hakkonen","name":"Hakkonen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-30T20:48:13-08:00","id":39758,"title":"","content":"Rivet Arm (pg. 198) does not have stats for distance. Not sure if that's a thing for this thread or not, but worth pointing out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1481-obviouspword","name":"ObviousPword","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-30T22:42:24-08:00","id":39800,"title":"","content":"page 87: The letter D in Demon isn't bold, just above Prelude: &quot;...in order to create a D<b>emon</b> character.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-30T23:01:51-08:00","id":39811,"title":"","content":"Found this in the section describing Inquisitors <br /> p.42 Because gathering information can be a slow process, Integrators(<b>Should be Inquisitors</b>) value their Covers.<br /> <br /> Detective Jack","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Madness doesn't howl. Madness is that little voice in your head that speaks to you at the end of the day and asks, &quot;Is there room for one more?&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/595-detective-jack-raines","name":"Detective Jack Raines","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar595_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T01:00:08-08:00","id":39851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ObviousPword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/38920-demon-errata?p=39758#post39758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rivet Arm (pg. 198) does not have stats for distance. Not sure if that's a thing for this thread or not, but worth pointing out.</div> </div> </div> </div> it's meant to be the same as a shotgun","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T03:09:58-08:00","id":39874,"title":"","content":"Page 37, paragraph 6: &quot;Although it can like an agonizing eternity....&quot; should probably be &quot;Although it can <b>feel</b> like an agonizing eternity....&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1860-teddyboy","name":"Teddyboy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T18:06:35-08:00","id":40269,"title":"","content":"The layers in the background don't seem to be working correctly in Chapter Three... or at least the background there is blocky on my computer and tablet in a way that it isn't in Chapters Two and Four.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/134196/Chuubos-Marvelous-WishGranting-Engine\" target=\"_blank\">Chuubo's Marvelous Wish-Granting Engine RPG</a> \u2014 <a href=\"http://www.patreon.com/JennaMoran\" target=\"_blank\">Jenna Moran's Patreon</a> \u2014 <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/215-rand-brittain","name":"Rand Brittain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T22:00:26-08:00","id":40348,"title":"","content":"Page 87 - Power select summary - the words psychopomp and mundane are inverted so to read psychopomp ( mundane ) instead of mundane ( psychopomp ).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>J. T. Legal</b><br /> The other kind of rules lawyer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/334-technocratjt","name":"TechnocratJT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar334_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-01T02:48:01-08:00","id":40432,"title":"","content":"Page 70 - Second Paragraph of the Fluff: &quot;<b>No few of those</b> scouts take their orders from the God-Machine.&quot;<br /> <br /> Page 100 - There's an alignment error for the text &quot;Unscheduled Demolition&quot; - Unscheduled has spread out over the entire line.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/38920-demon-errata?p=39851#post39851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> it's meant to be the same as a shotgun</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps that should be reflected in the text - I think I've seen you guys answer that question specifically a half-dozen times in various forum posts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1462,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","user":"Xenesis","date":". 01-01-2014, 06:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-01T15:56:25-08:00","id":40776,"title":"","content":"Also not sure if it belongs here:<br /> P. 206 aegis protocol when spending 1 aether there is no duration given for how long the armour function is in existence","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T04:01:05-08:00","id":41017,"title":"","content":"Page 205 - Under the entry for Wings: &quot;System: The demon is capable of flight and <b>has a species factor of 10 to his Speed</b> while flying.&quot;<br /> <br /> Page 224 - Under the entry for The Life Stigmatic: &quot;What\u2019s more, though stigmatics can now view the systems of reality<b>, and</b> the human mind is in no way designed to make sense of the enormous information overload.&quot;<br /> <br /> Page 224 - Every other sentence here has 2-3 commas, when most could be removed. It makes it a lot harder to read than necessary.<br /> <br /> Page 237 - The Blue Outline for &quot;Universal Machinery&quot; doesn't go far down enough - the bottom line of text edges over the bottom line of the box.<br /> <br /> Page 242 - The Blue Outline for the box &quot;First, decide what the God-Machine's objective is....&quot; - the bottom line of text edges over the bottom line of the box.<br /> <br /> Character Sheet - There's not quite enough contrast between the attribute dots when filled in and the background around them. It's hard to see whether you've that first dot filled in or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1462,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","user":"Xenesis","date":". 01-02-2014, 08:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T05:35:56-08:00","id":41054,"title":"","content":"Page 61, under the &quot;Infrastructure&quot; heading: &quot;And you can't have <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>those</b></span> unless you have a source...&quot; The word &quot;those&quot; is both bolded and in a larger font than the surrounding text. I'm not sure if it's an error or just overenthusiastic emphasis, but I haven't seen it anywhere else in the book; nor can I recall seeing it in other White Wolf/Onyx Path books. Also, don't start sentences with &quot;and.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1856-hakkonen","name":"Hakkonen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T22:51:07-08:00","id":41530,"title":"","content":"I had my notes on my iPad which just died.........<br /> <br /> But the first one picked up on the re-read-through is on Page 17, &quot;Chapter Two Characters and Traits&quot; needs a colon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Once is happenstance. Twice is coincidence. Three times is enemy action. Four times is Infrastructure.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> Rule #2: Never let the game-mechanics get in the way of a good story.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1642-paddon","name":"Paddon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1642_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T23:08:33-08:00","id":41539,"title":"","content":"&quot;Achievable Goals&quot; sidebar's first sentence (p47), &quot;Hell for the Company&quot; fourth sentence of second paragraph (p48), &quot;The Cipher&quot; sidebar's first sentence (p155): use of &quot;the reality&quot; instead of &quot;reality.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-04T07:58:53-08:00","id":42281,"title":"","content":"Page 80 These can also be used to buy Primum at the rate of one point for three Merit dots.<br /> Page 87 Merits dots may be spent to increase Primum (5 Merit dots = a dot of Primum).<br /> <br /> Page 330 Beat:Character fails to fulfill an obligation due to pursuing her <i><b>obligation</b></i>. under Obsession condition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1890-terry313","name":"Terry313","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T13:03:20-08:00","id":43079,"title":"","content":"Not a spelling error but still worth mentioning:<br /> Some of the sidebars have highlights in the background that make the text difficult to read.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://emeraldsamurai.com\" target=\"_blank\">Emerald Samurai</a> for my alternative character-sheets for WoD, Scion, Exalted and more.<br /> Like my <a href=\"http://www.facebook.com/EmeraldSamurai\" target=\"_blank\">Facebook page</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/308-skari-dono","name":"Skari-dono","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T01:19:00-08:00","id":44018,"title":"","content":"<b>Page 89</b>: Cover is listed as costing 2 Experiences, whereas it's listed as 3 elsewhere (and was said to be 3 in a few posts on the forums).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T09:41:16-08:00","id":44240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/38920-demon-errata?p=40432#post40432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Page 70 - Second Paragraph of the Fluff: &quot;<b>No few of those</b> scouts take their orders from the God-Machine.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;No few&quot; is a roundabout but grammatically correct synonym for &quot;many.&quot; There is no issue here.<br /> <br /> In the Character Creation Quick Reference Chart on pages 87-89, there are some stylistic issues.<ul><li>In the &quot;Choose 4 Embeds and/or Exploits&quot; step, the list reads: &quot;Cacophony (Destroyer), Instrumental (Guardian), Vocal (Messenger), <b>Psychopomp (Mundane)</b>. One of these things is not like the others.</li> <li>In the &quot;Select Merits&quot; step, consider making &quot;5 Merit dots = a dot of Primum&quot; &quot;5 Merit dots = 1 dot of Primum&quot; instead, for improved clarity.</li> <li>In the &quot;Calculate Advantages&quot; step, there's an awkward line break. &quot;Defense is (lower of Wits and Dexteri-ty...&quot; The word Dexterity should either not be hyphenated or be hyphenated after the first syllable (Dex-terity).</li> <li>At the end of the checklist, &quot;...in order to create a D<b>emon</b> character.&quot; Unbolded letter in a bolded word.</li> <li>Under the &quot;Incarnations&quot; heading, more strangely-placed line breaks, in &quot;...created by the God-Ma-chine&quot; and &quot;...scourge of the God-Ma-chine.&quot; The phrase, &quot;God-Machine,&quot; is already hyphenated; inserting additional hyphens is contraindicated. Also, in the phrase, &quot;target of their re-sponsibility,&quot; responsibility should not be hyphenated. It's only two characters, move the whole word to the next line.</li> <li>Under &quot;Agendas,&quot; &quot;...taking different ap-proaches...&quot; has the same problem.</li> <li>Under &quot;Merits,&quot; &quot;...as they already have these abilities by <b>de-fault by</b> default.&quot; Badly placed line break and redundant words. Fix by omitting the bolded words.</li> <li>Also under &quot;Merits,&quot; the phrase &quot;De-mon-specific&quot; has an extraneous line break. There's enough room on the line for the whole word &quot;Demon.&quot;</li> <li>Under &quot;Starting Experiences,&quot; in the first row of the table, &quot;5 Experience&quot; should be &quot;5 Experience<b>s</b>.&quot;</li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1856-hakkonen","name":"Hakkonen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T05:50:40-08:00","id":45527,"title":"","content":"Page 151 - The Dramatic Failure section of &quot;Marco Polo&quot;: &quot;The target stays silent and has a perfectly good <b>bead</b> on the demon&quot;.<br /> <br /> I'm assuming this is supposed to be &quot;lead&quot;, &quot;read&quot;, &quot;bearing&quot; or something similar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T06:47:44-08:00","id":45548,"title":"","content":"This is actually correct, &quot;getting a bead on someone&quot; is an actual phrase in English. It comes from firearm use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-10T14:13:35-08:00","id":46485,"title":"","content":"Lexicon and Index refer to Cacophony Embeds as &quot;Cacophonic Embeds&quot; and are the only places the latter word is used over the former.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-11T04:15:46-08:00","id":46827,"title":"","content":"P. 116, under &quot;Pacts,&quot; at the start of the second paragraph: &quot;When a demon makes a pact (see p. 116)...&quot; It's citing the Pacts section of page 116 <b>in the middle of the Pacts section of page 116.</b><br /> <br /> P. 156, under &quot;Final Secret:&quot; &quot;Rather, it is a <b>technognostic</b> truth...&quot; Presumably, that's meant to be &quot;techgnostic.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1856,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1856-hakkonen","user":"Hakkonen","date":". 01-11-2014, 08:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1856-hakkonen","name":"Hakkonen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T04:24:51-08:00","id":47320,"title":"","content":"I noticed this on RPG.net today: <a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?713855-Demon-Rules-Questions\" target=\"_blank\">Link</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Random Nerd</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> First, when you use your full demonic form, is the Compromise roll at -2 or -3? Page 113 says -3, but 195 says -2.</div> </div> </div> </div>I checked, and the numbers in the text don't match like he says.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T09:15:57-08:00","id":48222,"title":"","content":"In the description of the &quot;Frozen in Time&quot; Exploit, p. 167, it says, &quot;Gravity does not affect the character, either, meaning a target frozen in time while falling does not travel through space.&quot; This implies that a victim of this exploit would immediately (appear to) fly off the surface of the planet, as Earth moves on in its orbit and leaves the character behind. I doubt this is working as intended.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1856-hakkonen","name":"Hakkonen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T09:48:05-08:00","id":48257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hakkonen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/38920-demon-errata?p=48222#post48222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the description of the &quot;Frozen in Time&quot; Exploit, p. 167, it says, &quot;Gravity does not affect the character, either, meaning a target frozen in time while falling does not travel through space.&quot; This implies that a victim of this exploit would immediately (appear to) fly off the surface of the planet, as Earth moves on in its orbit and leaves the character behind. I doubt this is working as intended.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose that the intent of the rule here is that the target's position <i>relative to Earth</i> (or whatever realm of existence you're in) doesn't change. If you freeze a snowflake one meter above the ground at the geographic North Pole, it'll stay one meter above the ground at the geographic North Pole for as long as the Exploit is in effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Part-time table flipper.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/519-chairkicker","name":"ChairKicker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar519_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-14T05:56:22-08:00","id":48896,"title":"","content":"Thank you all for the errata comments. We'll be closing this thread so that we can do final implementation at <b>12:00 PM EST, Thursday January 16th</b>. Again, thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":2,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","user":"Rose Bailey","date":". 01-16-2014, 04:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-14T05:59:46-08:00","id":48898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChairKicker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/38920-demon-errata?p=48257#post48257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose that the intent of the rule here is that the target's position <i>relative to Earth</i> (or whatever realm of existence you're in) doesn't change. If you freeze a snowflake one meter above the ground at the geographic North Pole, it'll stay one meter above the ground at the geographic North Pole for as long as the Exploit is in effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that's the intent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-14T10:37:49-08:00","id":49110,"title":"","content":"It could be worded more clearly (and in a manner less prone to munchkinry). For example, instead of &quot;Gravity doesn't affect the character...&quot; say &quot;Characters frozen in time while falling remain suspended in midair for the duration of the effect.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1856-hakkonen","name":"Hakkonen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T08:12:03-08:00","id":49807,"title":"","content":"I hope it's not too late to submit this. I hoped to get through Chapter 1 before posting.<br /> <br /> First of all, I want to say I'm so glad Onyx Path got this out to the backers so we could help spot errors. It sounds really nerdy but highlighting and proofreading WoD books is more my hobby than playing the actual games. <br /> <br /> Sorry if I resubmit ones that were already said. Most of what I saw have to do with hyphens and commas, which are highly contextual and difficult for automated systems to pick up. The missing words &amp; spaces are probably the most important revisions though.<br /> <br /> <u>PDF formatting</u> -- The PDF bookmarks for all of chapter one are filed under &quot;To Serve in Heaven.&quot; I think the intention was to have the sub-bookmarks of Chapter 1 be (&quot;To Serve in Heaven,&quot; &quot;To Reign in Hell,&quot; &quot;Life as a Demon,&quot; &quot;Descent,&quot; &quot;Antagonists,&quot; &quot;Embedded Agents,&quot; and &quot;Infrastructure&quot;)<br /> <br /> <u>Incorrect word</u> -- p. 33 Second-to-last sentence of second-to-last paragraph before &quot;To Reign in Hell,&quot;: ... kept studded by constant recycling.&quot; should probably be &quot;...kept <b>stunted</b> by constant recycling.&quot;<br /> <br /> <u>Confusing</u> -- p. 33 Second sentence of first paragraph below &quot;To Reign in Hell&quot; reads: &quot;Images of his taut muscles, light brown skin and sharp laugh...&quot; laughing typically doesn't produce images. Perhaps the first word should be &quot;Memories&quot;<br /> <br /> <u>Missing space</u> -- p. 34 First sentence under Guardian: &quot;...something in orderto ensure...&quot; missing a space between &quot;order&quot; and &quot;to&quot;<br /> <br /> Not mistake, just a <u>suggestion</u> -- p. 35 Under Inquisitor, the phrase &quot;ahead of the day when&quot; is used twice in quick succession (adding &quot;inevitable&quot; doesn't reduce the repetitiveness). I would change one to &quot;long before&quot; or something similar.<br /> <br /> possible <u>Extra word</u> -- p. 35 Last sentence of Tempter uses the phrase, &quot;cult of the personality,&quot; I've never heard it with a &quot;the.&quot; The Wikipedia article is &quot;Cult of Personality&quot; so that's what I'd go with.<br /> <br /> <u>Confusing</u> -- p. 36 Third paragraph below &quot;Why We Fall&quot;, second sentence: &quot;The contradictions inherent in being an angel \u2014 obedient but independent, detached but objective&quot; Obedience and independence can oppose one another but detachment and objectivity are usually considered complementary traits.<br /> <br /> <u>Missing word</u> -- p. 36 Fifth paragraph below &quot;Why We Fall&quot;, fourth sentence: &quot;He starts to defy orders small ways...&quot; Should be &quot;He starts to defy orders in small ways...&quot;<br /> <br /> <u>Extra comma?</u> -- p. 36 right-hand column, second paragraph from the top, last sentence: &quot;talk to a human without lying to them, once in a while&quot; The comma between &quot;them&quot; and &quot;once&quot; seems unnecessary to me since it's still part of the clause.<br /> <br /> <u>Missing hyphen</u> -- p. 36 right-hand column, third paragraph, third sentence: &quot;...angels are well aware...&quot; well-aware is usually hyphenated, like well-liked and well-respected.<br /> <br /> <u>Extra space</u> -- p. 36 last sentence of second-to-last paragraph: &quot;...kill him on sight .&quot; unnecessary space between &quot;sight&quot; and the period.<br /> <br /> <u>Missing word</u> -- p. 37 First sentence of second-to-last paragraph: &quot;Although it can like an agonizing eternity...&quot; Needs a verb between &quot;can&quot; and &quot;like&quot;. Should perhaps read: &quot;Although it can <b>feel</b> like an agonizing eternity...&quot;<br /> <br /> <u>Plural error</u> -- p. 39 Last sentence of first paragraph in the &quot;With Fallen Scales&quot; sidebar: &quot;...a city of hundreds of thousand humans...&quot; A more conventional phrasing would be &quot;...a city of hundreds of <b>thousands</b> humans...&quot;<br /> <br /> <u>Wrong/missing word</u> -- p. 39 first sentence of third paragraph under &quot;The Mask&quot;: &quot;...whatever it takes together impressionable humans...&quot; should probably read as &quot;...whatever it takes <b>to gather</b> impressionable humans...&quot;<br /> <br /> <u>Missing comma</u> -- p. 40 Under &quot;Cover and Identity&quot;, sixth paragraph, last sentence: &quot;...Cover is a matter of life and death and identity is rarely more than a matter of convenience.&quot; Life and death is a phrase, but I would definitely put a comma before &quot;identity&quot; to help with clarity.<br /> <br /> <u>Missing space</u> -- p. 40 last sentence of second paragraph in the right-hand column: &quot;...saving moneyor undertaking...&quot; space needed between &quot;money&quot; and &quot;or&quot;<br /> <br /> <u>Suggestion</u> -- p. 40 last sentence of third paragraph in the right-hand column: &quot;If a demon wants to lead a totally different kind of life...&quot; Not grammatically necessary but beginning the sentence with &quot;However&quot; or &quot;But&quot; might make it read a bit better.<br /> <br /> <u>Hyphenate?</u> -- p. 40 second-to-last sentence of second-to-last paragraph in the right-hand column: &quot;...step into a fully realized human life.&quot; Seem like there should be a hyphen in &quot;fully realized&quot;<br /> <br /> <u>Extra word</u> -- p. 41 First sentence under &quot;Incarnation, Agenda, and Humanity&quot;: &quot;...the Covers that let them walk seem like humans.&quot; Either &quot;walk&quot; or &quot;seem&quot; should be kept, but not both.<br /> <br /> <u>Missing comma</u> -- p. 41 Second sentence under &quot;Incarnation, Agenda, and Humanity&quot;: &quot;In part this is because&quot; Ought to be a comma between &quot;part&quot; and &quot;this&quot;<br /> <br /> <u>Missing hyphen</u> -- p. 41 second-to-last sentence of second-to last paragraph before the &quot;Psychopomps&quot; header: &quot;...and a short tempered Destroyer...&quot; Should be a hyphen in &quot;short tempered&quot; especially noticeable because &quot;short-tempered&quot; is correctly hyphenated earlier in the sentence.<br /> <br /> <u>Missing hyphen</u> -- p. 42 third sentence after &quot;Inquisitors&quot;: &quot;...a side effect of spending...&quot; Should have a hyphen between &quot;side&quot; and &quot;effect&quot;<br /> <br /> <u>Missing word?</u> -- p. 42 Last sentence of last paragraph before &quot;Integrators&quot;: &quot;They believe that they tread lightly...&quot; Do you mean &quot;They believe that they <b>should</b> tread lightly...&quot;<br /> <br /> <u>Missing parenthetical/commas?</u> -- p. 42 Last sentence of last paragraph before &quot;Integrators&quot;: &quot;...and for<br /> better or worse they will never...&quot; I usually see the phrase &quot;for better or worse&quot; offset by commas or parentheses.<br /> <br /> <u>Wrong punctuation</u> -- p. 43 Second paragraph after &quot;Fallen Flesh&quot;: third/fourth sentence: &quot;...chosen human death, They hope that...&quot; The phrasing and random capital letter make it fairly clear this comma was meant to be a period.<br /> <br /> <u>Incorrect plural</u> -- p. 43 First sentence of fourth paragraph after &quot;Fallen Flesh&quot;: &quot;...spend most of their times hiding...&quot; Should be just &quot;time&quot; instead of &quot;times&quot;<br /> <br /> <u>Missing hyphen</u> -- p. 43 Second sentence of sixth paragraph after &quot;Fallen Flesh&quot;: &quot;...terrifying shape, hard pressed to find mortals...&quot; Most dictionaries I've seen hyphenate &quot;hard-pressed&quot;<br /> <br /> <u>Extra word</u> -- p. 44 First sentence under &quot;Fallen Mind&quot; &quot;...emotional outlook is resembles that of a human...&quot; Don't need &quot;is&quot; between &quot;outlook&quot; and &quot;resembles&quot;<br /> <br /> <u>Unnecessary capitalization?</u> -- p. 44 Second and third sentences after &quot;Fallen Heart&quot; both capitalize Demon in the middle of the sentence. Not technically wrong, but inconsistent with the convention of the rest of the book.<br /> <br /> <u>Missing commas</u> -- p. 45 second paragraph, third sentence: &quot;The slender Polynesian woman you speak to on Thursday could be a bearded six-and-a-half foot tall white guy on the following Tuesday.&quot; There should probably be commas or conjunctions between a bunch of these adjectives. &quot;bearded six-and-a-half foot tall white&quot; should definitely have at least one comma (maybe two) and possibly also between &quot;slender&quot; and &quot;Polynesian&quot; because they're both being used as adjectives here.<br /> <br /> <u>Missing word + missing hyphen?</u> -- p. 45 Last sentence before &quot;What Do Demons Do All Day?&quot;: &quot;It\u2019s almost impossible to be sure that a given demon is true believer...&quot; First of all, we need an &quot;a&quot; between &quot;is&quot; and &quot;true.&quot; Second, I usually hyphenate &quot;true-believer&quot; but then I might be a bit overzealous about hyphenating two-word terms.<br /> <br /> <u>Missing word</u> -- p. 45 Last sentence in the third paragraph from the bottom reads: &quot;...demons come feel the same way...&quot; should read &quot;...demons come <b>to</b> feel the same way...&quot;<br /> <br /> <u>Missing hyphen</u> -- p. 45 Second sentence of last paragraph: &quot;commitment of a full time job.&quot; Full-time is usually hyphenated.<br /> <br /> <u>Suggestion</u> -- Were it me, I'd visually differentiate the example stories at the beginning of sections like &quot;I Saw Satan Fall Like Lightning&quot; and &quot;What Do Demons Do All Day?&quot; from the rest of the text, such as having it in italics. I seem to remember the core World of Darkness and other books formatting it like that.<br /> <br /> <u>Missing comma</u> -- p. 51 First paragraph after Exiles, third sentence: &quot;In some cases the occult matrix...&quot; comma missing? Shouldn't it be &quot;In some cases, the occult matrix...&quot;?<br /> <br /> <u>Missing commas</u> -- p. 57 Second complete paragraph from the top, first sentence: &quot;A lone demon quietly making the best of her new life surrounds herself with humanity but is not truly a part of it.&quot; Shouldn't the phrase &quot;quietly making the best of her new life&quot; be offset with commas?<br /> <br /> <u>Missing comma</u> -- p. 58 Under Insurgent Agencies, first paragraph, fourth sentence: &quot;Lesser demons tend to have difficulty convincing potential early recruits...&quot; missing a comma between potential and early?<br /> <br /> <u>Missing comma</u> -- p. 58 Under Compromised Agencies, third paragraph, second sentence: &quot;In almost all cases a compromised Agency...&quot; Should probably be &quot;In almost all cases<b>,</b> a compromised Agency...&quot;<br /> <br /> <u>Incorrect word</u> -- p. 112 Under Initial Cover, first paragraph, fourth sentence: &quot;...hate the Cover identity they began with, thought, seeing it as a last sign...&quot; should be &quot;...hate the Cover identity they began with, <b>though</b>, seeing it as a last sign...&quot;<br /> <br /> <u>Extra word</u> -- p. 195 Under Demonic Forms, Full Transformation, first paragraph, first sentence: &quot;Changing into demonic form is requires very little effort.&quot; the word &quot;is&quot; should probably be removed<br /> <br /> <u>Missing comma?</u> -- p. 195 Under Demonic Forms, Full Transformation, first paragraph, &quot;...health box upon changing into her demonic form.&quot; Comma missing between 'box' and 'upon'<br /> <br /> <u>Wrong word</u> -- p. 195 Under Demonic Forms, Full Transformation, third paragraph, third sentence: &quot;Regardless of the presence on onlookers&quot; the word &quot;on&quot; should probably be replaced with &quot;of&quot; or &quot;of any&quot;<br /> <br /> <u>Hyphenate</u> -- p. 197 Under Blade Hand, second sentence: &quot;...allowing for nothing more than routine maintenance to keep them well honed.&quot; I would hyphenate well-honed just like well-known and well-kept.<br /> <br /> <u>Wrong word</u> -- p. 205 Under Wings, first sentence: &quot;...whether its the need to get to high places...&quot; Classic mistake we've all made. Should read, &quot;...whether <b>it's</b> the need to get to high places...&quot;<br /> <br /> <u>Wrong word</u> -- p. 205 Under Processes, Aegis Protocol, System, second sentence: &quot;...but does not impart an penalty to his Initiative.&quot; This should probably read, &quot;...but does not impart <b>any</b> penalty to his Initiative.&quot; or &quot;...but does not impart <b>a</b> penalty to his Initiative.&quot;<br /> <br /> <u>Suggestion</u> -- The Appearance for Magnesium Flare (p. 206) reads more like the specifications of the System than as suggestions for how it could appear. That said, the appearance and system are sort of one and the same for this.<br /> <br /> <u>Confusing</u> -- The Dice Pool for Memory Theft (p. 207) is &quot;Manipulation + Subterfuge - Composure&quot;. I assume this means to subtract the target's Composure. If that's the case, it would likely help with clarity to say so. I couldn't come up with a reason why a demon with high Composure should be worse at this.<br /> <br /> <u>Conjugation</u> -- p. 207 Under Quill Burst, second sentence: &quot;...fitted with a self-defense mechanism that allow them...&quot; should be &quot;...fitted with a self-defense mechanism that <b>allows</b> them...&quot;<br /> <br /> <u>Spacing</u> -- p. 208 Under Rain of Fire, Success, last sentence: &quot;...only remain for one turn/ Primum dot.&quot; There is a space only on the right side of the '/' which doesn't fit the style of the rest of the book.<br /> <br /> <u>Wrong word</u> -- p. 208 Under Voice of the Angel, third sentence: &quot;...are still capable to sending electronic signals.&quot; Should be &quot;...are still capable <b>of</b> sending electronic signals.&quot;<br /> <br /> <u>Hyphenate?</u> -- p. 208 Under Voice of the Angel, System: &quot;...letting out an ear piercing screech...&quot; Should be &quot;...letting out an <b>ear-piercing</b> screech...&quot;<br /> <br /> <u>Confusing</u> -- The Dice pool for Voice of the Angel, isn't in its own separate &quot;Dice Pool:&quot; section. Also it has a similar phrasing issue as Memory Theft where &quot;- Composure&quot; seems to suggest you subtract the demon's Composure. Unless that's the intended meaning.<br /> <br /> Hope this helps. I just leapt at the opportunity to help make a World of Darkness book better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1925-toroid","name":"Toroid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1925_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan